Komorebi source provenance
=========================

yespower 1.0.1 (upstream 1977c28)
Repository: https://github.com/openwall/yespower
Commit: 1977c283bc43eed5a2c2579e02d6d996e49866b0

The vendored C sources, headers and README are unmodified upstream files
from this pinned commit. Only files needed by the production implementation
and its documentation are included; use the upstream checkout for make check.
The yespower-1.0.1 directory name is retained for build/include stability.

Previously these files were copied from sugarchain-project/sugarchain commit
64bc05ccc1dc2dcd4db9e86715c14dee12be6460 and were byte-identical to Openwall's
YESPOWER_1_0_1 release (d81b48a5793ceaffcf34079df9d446b752a3e113).

This is an implementation update, not a consensus algorithm change.
YespowerSugar still uses YESPOWER_1_0, N=2048, r=32 and the 74-byte string:
Satoshi Nakamoto 31/Oct/2008 Proof-of-work is essentially one-CPU-one-vote
Header serialization, output byte order, PoW comparison and validation
call sites are unchanged. No local performance patches or hash cache are
added. Upstream copyright, license and attribution remain in each file.

Komorebi uses its existing CMake compiler options, not the upstream Makefile
flags. This update does not add -march=native or enable additional instruction
sets.
